                <pb facs="0618" n="516" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg516"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">819.6156 T 61/11: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Panama</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >South</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-06-03T14:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 3, 1927—2
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>42. Your despatch 1413, May 14. In reply to Government’s note you may inform
                    Secretary of Foreign Affairs that the position of the United States has not in
                    any way changed since the presentation of the Legation’s note of March 3,
                    1921.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
